# Read by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. NOT read by GitHub Pages, which serves
# no custom headers at all -- see .github/workflows/pages.yml.
#
# The first two are the reason this file is load-bearing rather than
# defence-in-depth. Cross-origin isolation is what makes SharedArrayBuffer
# available, and SharedArrayBuffer is what makes whisper.cpp run threaded. On a
# host that drops these headers the app still works and is several times slower;
# site/main.js reads `crossOriginIsolated` and is expected to pick a
# single-threaded build rather than fail.
#
# require-corp is the strict half: every cross-origin subresource must opt in.
# That is why the wasm binary is served from this origin (src/core/engine.js) --
# and why model downloads from Hugging Face need its CORS headers to keep
# working, which is a dependency on someone else's configuration and worth
# knowing about before it breaks.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
